course: dictionary
lesson: 6105
title: Words that sound like what they mean
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound like the thing they name. Miaow is one of them: say it out loud and you can hear a cat. Words like this are called onomatopoeia, which means a word that sounds like its meaning.
explain: Miaow can be a noun, a verb or an exclamation. A miaow is the sound a cat makes. To miaow is to make that sound. «The cat miaowed at the back door.» Here miaowed is a verb, because it tells you what the cat did.
explain: Other languages use their own sound words for animals. In French, a cat says «miaou», and a duck says «coin-coin». When you meet a sound word, say it aloud and listen for the clue in its sound.
fact: Miaow is a word that sounds like the sound it describes.
fact: A miaow is the sound a cat makes; to miaow means to make that sound.
fact: Miaow can also be used as an exclamation, as in «Miaow!»
fact: French animal noises: «ouaf ouaf» (woof woof), «miaou» (miaow), «cocorico» (cock-a-doodle-doo), «meuh» (moo), «coin-coin» (quack quack).
fact: Onomatopoeia is a word that sounds like its meaning, such as miaow, woof or moo.
exercise: What is a miaow? | A small bed for a kitten | A cat with a very long tail | A kind of cat food | *The sound a cat makes
exercise: «The cat miaowed at the back door.» What kind of word is miaowed here? | A word for a place | A question word | A noun, a name for a thing | *A verb, an action word for what the cat did
exercise: Which word sounds like its own meaning? | Ancient | *Miaow | Happy | Table
test: What is onomatopoeia? | *A word that sounds like what it means | A word that means the opposite of another word | A word taken from French only | A long word with many syllables
test: In French, «meuh» is the sound of which animal? | Duck | Dog | Cockerel | *Cow
exam: Which of these is an example of onomatopoeia? | Ancient | Table | *Miaow | Happy
